    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/ext-ag-agent-nmsu-satellite-location-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Ext Ag Agent",
      "description": "Ext Ag Agent - NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Ext Ag Agent 504049 NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist Closing at: Oct 4 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Monica Lury, 505-983-4615, northern@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The Cooperative Extension Service at New Mexico State University invites applications for an Extension 4-H Agriculture and Natural Resources Agent. The successful candidate will provide leadership in Agriculture and Natural Resources education while directing a vibrant 4-H Youth Development program that prepares the next generation of agricultural leaders. Position Details Position Title: Ext Ag Agent College/Division: Cooperative Extension Service Department: 312600-ADMIN PRGM TORRANCE CTY Location: NMSU satellite location Offsite Location (if applicable): Torrance County, Estancia NM Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $62,000 commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Shift: Other Shift If Not a Standard Work Schedule: May work evenings and weekends Job Duties and Responsibilities: **This is Non-Tenure Track. POSITION IS LOCATED in Estancia, NM** The Cooperative Extension Service seeks a dynamic and innovative Extension Agent to provide leadership for Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) and 4-H Youth Development programming. The Agent will develop, implement, and evaluate educational programs addressing agriculture, natural resource management, livestock production, crop production, water conservation and use, rangeland stewardship, and related agricultural issues. A major responsibility is leadership of the county 4-H Youth Development Program, engaging youth and adult volunteers in experiential learning opportunities that develop life skills, leadership capacity, workforce readiness, and agricultural literacy. • Assess community needs and develop educational programs in agriculture and natural resources. • Deliver research-based education related to livestock production, crop production, water conservation and irrigation, soil health, rangeland management, sustainability, and agricultural economics. • Provide leadership and educational support related to land and water use issues impacting agricultural communities. • Provide overall leadership for the county 4-H Youth Development Program with emphasis on Agriculture and Natural Resources. • Recruit, train, mentor, and support adult and youth volunteers. • Organize and support 4-H clubs, camps, contests, workshops, fairs, leadership events, and experiential learning activities. • Serve as advisor and chaperone at county, district, state, and national 4-H events. • Collaborate with schools, youth-serving organizations, agencies, and community partners. • Support county fairs, livestock shows, and Extension educational events. • Prepare required reports and support LEADS 2025 strategic initiatives. • Work flexible schedules and travel as necessary. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Master's degree (in hand by hire date) required. At least one degree must be in Agriculture or a related field. Or may be underfilled as an Extension Associate I (Entry $52,000 commensurate with qualifications). Bachelor's degree in Agriculture or related field with a cumulative 2.5 GPA or higher required. Must complete a master's degree within 5 years of hire date to continue employment. Promotion to assistant professor rank will be based on performance and Dean's approval. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree preferred in Agriculture, Agricultural Education, Animal Science, Range Science, Natural Resource Management, Agronomy, Water Resources, Youth Development, Extension Education, or a related field. Experience in Cooperative Extension, agricultural education, youth development, or a related field. Knowledge of livestock production, crop systems, water management, rangelands, soil health, and sustainable agriculture. Experience working with agricultural producers and rural communities. Familiarity with the 4-H Youth Development Program and positive youth development principles. Experience recruiting, training, and managing volunteers. Strong oral and written communication skills and ability to work with diverse audiences. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work involves moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds or standing and/or walking for more than four (4) hours per day. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 4e9f5341 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 312600-ADMIN PRGM TORRANCE CTY 312600-ADMIN PRGM TORRANCE CTY Locations NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) e5dd1a3e Last Name (required) b362fb3a Email (required) 65d1bbff Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor, Communication Disorders Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 350600-COMMUNICATION DISORDERS The Department of Communication Disorders in the College of Health, Education, and Social Transformation invites applications for one 9-month, tenure-track position as assistant professor with an anticipated start date of either January 2027 or August 2027. The department offers undergraduate and graduate instruction for approximately 300 students. The successful candidate will join a collegial, supportive, and student-centered faculty and is expected to teach, perform research, and provide service to the department, college, and the university. Regular on-campus presence and in-person job duties are required. Accountant Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 530410-RESTRICTED ACCOUNTING Join the Restricted Accounting team at New Mexico State University! This position offers an opportunity to contribute to NMSU's mission in a dynamic higher education environment. Director Banking Investments and Tax Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 530465-ACCOUNTING & FINANCIAL REPORTING Join the Accounting & Financial Reporting team at New Mexico State University! This position offers an opportunity to contribute to NMSU's mission in a dynamic higher education environment. College Asst Prof Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330350-BIOLOGY The Department of Biology is seeking a College Assistant Professor. Administrative Assistant Associate 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940880-DACC SCIENCE, ENGINEERING, MATH DIV DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Multi Media Specialist II Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 310000-COOPERATIVE EXTENSION SERVICE The Social Media Specialist is responsible for planning, creating, and executing a comprehensive social media strategy for outreach for the New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension Service (CES) and Agricultural Experiment Station (AES). This position strengthens public awareness of Extension and research programs, amplifies research-based information, and supports outreach, engagement, and reputation-building efforts across diverse audiences including producers, families, communities, youth, students, policymakers, and partners.\nThe Social Media Specialist works closely with educational media designers, Extension specialists, county offices, researchers, Ag Science Center faculty and staff, communicators, and leadership to translate complex information into engaging, accessible, and audience-centered social media content. Apply Now First Name (required) ee7be5cd Last Name (required) 125cae01 Email (required) f2ce08c3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/ext-ag-4h-agent-nmsu-satellite-location-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Ext Ag/4H Agent",
      "description": "Ext Ag/4H Agent - NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Ext Ag/4H Agent 504035 NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist Closing at: Oct 4 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Tom Dean, 575-646-2584, tdean@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Doña Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Position Details Position Title: Ext Ag/4H Agent College/Division: Cooperative Extension Service Department: 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY Location: NMSU satellite location Offsite Location (if applicable): Dona Ana County Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Shift: Other Shift If Not a Standard Work Schedule: May work on weekends and evenings Job Duties and Responsibilities: ** THIS IS A NON-TENURE TRACK POSITION ** *** POSITION IS PHYSICALLY LOCATED IN DONA ANA COUNTY, NM *** Successful candidate will: - Provide leadership and guidance to Extension educational programs for adults and youth including 4-H and youth, special interest groups, adult and youth leaders and the public throughout the county as the job requires. - Collaborate with youth serving community organizations and agencies to help further Extension 4-H Youth Development programs. - Support annual County Fair efforts. Recruit, train and support volunteer adult and youth leaders. - Team with other Extension Agents in the county and district and with State Specialists, District Department Head and Administrators in planning and implementing total Extension programs. - Maintain a favorable public image and gain acceptance for self, Extension and New Mexico State University among the county citizens. - Administratively responsible to the County Program Director and through him/her to the Southern District Department Head. - Provide timely reports as required. - Promote CES programs within the district to meet the LEADS 2025 goals prioritizing the program expansion to non-traditional demographics. - Foster collaborations and participate in activities and on research teams that support the work of the Center of Excellence in Food and Sustainable Agriculture (CESFAS). - The Extension 4-H/Ag Agent is responsible to travel county wide via personal vehicle to execute educational programming to the stakeholders of New Mexico. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Master's degree (in hand by hire date) required. At least one degree must be in Agriculture or a related field. Or may be underfilled as an Extension Associate I (Entry $52,000 commensurate with qualifications). Bachelor's degree in Agriculture or related field with a cumulative 2.5 GPA or higher required. Must complete a master's degree within 5 years of hire date to continue employment. Promotion to assistant professor rank will be based on performance and Dean's approval. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Special Certification/Licensure: Must live in the county where employed and willing to work odd hours as needed. Personal auto required: reimbursed at IRS rates per mile. Valid driver's license required. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed indoors. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds or standing and/or walking for more than four (4) hours per day. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to 