s) 54 Staff Part-time (1 items) 1 Temporary Faculty (5 items) 5 Temporary Staff (3 items) 3 City Search cities 6 filter options found City Alamogordo Community College (1 items) 1 Doña Ana Community College (11 items) 11 Grants Community College (3 items) 3 Las Cruces (55 items) 55 NMSU satellite location (13 items) 13 Remote Locations (5 items) 5 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor, Communication Disorders Las Cruces 350600-COMMUNICATION DISORDERS Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Communication Disorders in the College of Health, Education, and Social Transformation invites applications for one 9-month, tenure-track position as assistant professor with an anticipated start date of either January 2027 or August 2027. The department offers undergraduate and graduate instruction for approximately 300 students. The successful candidate will join a collegial, supportive, and student-centered faculty and is expected to teach, perform research, and provide service to the department, college, and the university. Regular on-campus presence and in-person job duties are required. Read more Accountant Senior Las Cruces 530410-RESTRICTED ACCOUNTING Staff Staff Full-time Join the Restricted Accounting team at New Mexico State University! This position offers an opportunity to contribute to NMSU's mission in a dynamic higher education environment. Read more Director Banking Investments and Tax Las Cruces 530465-ACCOUNTING & FINANCIAL REPORTING Staff Staff Full-time Join the Accounting & Financial Reporting team at New Mexico State University! This position offers an opportunity to contribute to NMSU's mission in a dynamic higher education environment. Read more College Asst Prof Las Cruces 330350-BIOLOGY Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Biology is seeking a College Assistant Professor. Read more Administrative Assistant Associate Doña Ana Community College 940880-DACC SCIENCE, ENGINEERING, MATH DIV Staff Staff Full-time DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Read more Multi Media Specialist II Las Cruces 310000-COOPERATIVE EXTENSION SERVICE Staff Staff Full-time The Social Media Specialist is responsible for planning, creating, and executing a comprehensive social media strategy for outreach for the New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension Service (CES) and Agricultural Experiment Station (AES). This position strengthens public awareness of Extension and research programs, amplifies research-based information, and supports outreach, engagement, and reputation-building efforts across diverse audiences including producers, families, communities, youth, students, policymakers, and partners.\nThe Social Media Specialist works closely with educational media designers, Extension specialists, county offices, researchers, Ag Science Center faculty and staff, communicators, and leadership to translate complex information into engaging, accessible, and audience-centered social media content. Read more Custodial Worker Senior Las Cruces 500695-FS CUSTODIAL SERVICES Staff Staff Full-time Facilities and Services is looking for a Custodial Worker, Senior to join and support the leadership team! Apply today! Read more Financial Aid Specialist Las Cruces 521040-UNIV FIN AID & SCHOLARSHIP SVCS Staff Staff Full-time The University Financial Aid and Scholarship Services Department is seeking a dependable, highly motivated student centered individual with excellent customer services skills to join the Financial Aid Team. Read more Registrar Admission Specialist Grants Community College 950850-GRCC STUDENT SERVICES CTR Staff Staff Full-time NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Read more Financial Aid Advisor Remote Locations 440100-NMSU GLOBAL Staff Staff Full-time Travel Requirements: Occasional travel and participation in in-person events may be required to support student and program success.\nLocation Preference: Candidates residing in New Mexico are preferred but not required. This remote position may be performed from most U.S. locations with a dedicated, distraction-free workspace and reliable high-speed internet access.\nWork Eligibility: This position is not eligible for employment in CA, CO, IN, NJ, NY, OH, OR, PA, WA, or MN.\n\nNew Mexico State University Global Campus seeks three Financial Aid Advisors, Univ. to serve as the primary resource for financial aid eligibility, compliance, and funding opportunities while providing guidance on federal, state, institutional, and private aid programs, reviewing applications, determining eligibility, assisting with appeals and academic plans, and supporting student success. Read more Program Specialist Senior Las Cruces 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES Staff Staff Full-time The Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences at New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Specialist, Senior to support the Floriculture Program. This position will provide coordination and technical support for floriculture education, lesson plans research and outreach activities. The successful candidate will assist with greenhouse and plant production operations, maintain and manage plant materials and facilities, coordinate program activities, and support faculty, students, and other stakeholders. Read more Ext Ag Agent NMSU satellite location 312600-ADMIN PRGM TORRANCE CTY Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist The Cooperative Extension Service at New Mexico State University invites applications for an Extension 4-H Agriculture and Natural Resources Agent. The successful candidate will provide leadership in Agriculture and Natural Resources education while directing a vibrant 4-H Youth Development program that prepares the next generation of agricultural leaders. Read more Ext Ag/4H Agent NMSU satellite location 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Doña Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement.\nThe successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Read more Administrative Assistant Associate Las Cruces 350150-CURRICULUM AND INSTRUCTION Staff Staff Full-time New Mexico State University College of HEST seeks an Administrative Assistant Associate. Read more Accountant Intermediate Las Cruces 470580-PSL BUSINESS ACCOUNTING OFFICE Staff Staff Full-time Join the PSL Accounting team as an Accountant Intermediate. Read more Assistant Manager Farm Ranch NMSU satellite location 302650-CLAYTON LIVESTOCK RES CTR Staff Staff Full-time The Clayton Livestock Research Center invites you to apply for the Assistant Manager, Farm Ranch position. This research center conducts science-based research to improve the health and performance of newly received cattle. Read more Student Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces 380001-GRADUATE SCHOOL Staff Staff Full-time The Graduate School is seeking a detail-oriented and organized Student Program Coordinator, Sr. to support graduate students throughout their academic journey, from admission through graduation. This position processes and maintains student records and documentation related to admissions, academic milestones, program requirements, final examinations, thesis and dissertation submission, and degree certification. The successful candidate will work closely with students, faculty, and academic departments to interpret requirements, resolve record and processing issues, and ensure accurate and timely completion of Graduate School processes. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, sound judgment, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential for success in this role. Read more Assistant Professor/Ornamental & Landscape Horticulture Las Cruces 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences (PES) at New Mexico State University (NMSU) is searching for a new faculty member in Horticulture with an emphasis on Ornamental and Landscape Horticulture. Read more College Assistant Professor Las Cruces 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Computer Science is seeking a College Assistant Professor. Read more Assistant or Associate Professor Social Work Las Cruces 370300-SOCIAL WORK Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Assistant or Associate Professor — School of Social Work New Mexico State University. The NMSU School of Social Work, part of the College of Health, Education, and Social Transformation, invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor faculty position at the Associate or Full Professor level. We're seeking a scholar-educator who can teach across our undergraduate and graduate curriculum — in person, online synchronous, and online asynchronous — grounded in CSWE/EPAS competencies. The ideal candidate brings an active, fundable research agenda, a strong record of mentoring students, and a genuine commitment to equity-centered social work education.\n\nRank and tenure status will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and record of scholarship, teaching, and service.\n\nNMSU is a Hispanic-Serving Institution with deep ties to Native American communities across the Southwest; candidates with experience in culturally responsive pedagogy, Indigenous social work practice, bilingual (Spanish/English) proficiency, and academic leadership are especially encouraged to apply. Required: PhD in Social Work; MSW from a CSWE-accredited program; teaching experience across delivery formats; a research agenda complementing existing faculty strengths; and a demonstrated commitment to DEI. To apply: Submit a letter of interest, CV, teaching philosophy, research statement, three references, and unofficial transcripts. Read more Assistant Professor, Ethnic Studies and Native American Studies Las Cruces 100272-BORDERLANDS AND ETHNIC STUDIES Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Borderlands and Ethnic Studies Department at New Mexico State University seeks a Tenure Track Assistant Professor who is qualified to teach courses in Ethnic Studies and Native American Studies, preferably through a broad Borderlands lens.\nIdeal candidates will have a Ph.D. in Ethnic Studies or Native American Studies; have the skills and knowledge to contribute to further developing curriculum and events/programming in Ethnic Studies and Native American Studies; and contribute to student-focused recruitment and retention strategies in the department; including continuing to forge partnerships with NMSU’s American Indian Programs student services unit as well as other related units across campus. Read more Assistant Professor, Ethnic Studies and Chicana/o Studies Las Cruces 100272-BORDERLANDS AND ETHNIC STUDIES Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The College of Health, Education, and Social Transformation has a job opening for a Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Borderlands and Ethnic Studies – Chicana/o Studies for the Borderlands and Ethnic Studies Department to begin Fall 2027. Read more Assistant Professor – Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Read more Instructor, HVAC Doña Ana Community College 940802-DACC HEATING AC AND REFRIG PGM Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Read more Asst Prof Las Cruces 330350-BIOLOGY Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Biology is seeking applicants for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor whose research focuses on the interactions between symbiotic or pathogenic microbes and their animal hosts. Applicants with expertise in the use of mammalian models are especially desirable. Read more Assistant Professor Education Grants Community College 950510-GRCC REG ACADEMIC INSTRUCTION Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Read more Assistant Professor of Nematology Las Cruces 303000-ENTOMOLOGY PLANT PATH AND WEED SCI Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Entomology, Plant Pathology, and Weed Science seeks to hire an Assistant Professor to develop an innovative, fundamental, and applied research program in nematology related to integrated pest management in the semi-arid west and teach courses needed by the Department and the College Read more Associate/Professor of Weed Science NMSU satellite location 317600-AG SCIENCE CTR AT CLOVIS Faculty 12-Month Faculty Full-Time New Mexico State University’s Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) seeks a 12-month Associate Professor or Professor faculty member to be stationed at the Clovis Agricultural Science Center located in Clovis, New Mexico. Read more Assistant Professor Las Cruces 330650-CRIMINAL JUSTICE Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Criminal Justice at New Mexico State University invites applications for one tenure-track Assistant Professor Position beginning August 16, 2027. Read more College Assistant Professor Automotive Grants Community College 950520-GRCC VOCATIONAL INSTRUCTION Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 88 in total ‹ 1 2 3 › Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then