NESIOLOGY (1 items) 1 350600-COMMUNICATION DISORDERS (1 items) 1 360200-CARLSBAD ENV MONITORING AND RES CTR (1 items) 1 370200-NURSING (1 items) 1 370300-SOCIAL WORK (1 items) 1 380001-GRADUATE SCHOOL (1 items) 1 440100-NMSU GLOBAL (2 items) 2 440410-DIGITAL LEARNING (1 items) 1 450270-IT DATABASE ADMINISTRATION (1 items) 1 470001-RESEARCH, CREATIVITY AND ED (1 items) 1 470300-RESEARCH ADMINISTRATION (1 items) 1 470580-PSL BUSINESS ACCOUNTING OFFICE (1 items) 1 470725-PSL TELEMETRY MISSILE SYSTEMS (1 items) 1 480200-UNIVERSITY GENERAL COUNSEL (1 items) 1 500300-POLICE DEPARTMENT NMSU (4 items) 4 500425-FIRE PROTECTION SERVICES (1 items) 1 500450-FS ACCOUNTING (1 items) 1 500695-FS CUSTODIAL SERVICES (1 items) 1 500770-FS MECHANICAL (3 items) 3 510100-OFFICE OF PEOPLE RELATIONS (1 items) 1 521010-UNDERGRAD ADMISSIONS & ORIENTATION (1 items) 1 521040-UNIV FIN AID & SCHOLARSHIP SVCS (2 items) 2 522000-CORPORATE RELATIONS & CAREER EVENTS (1 items) 1 523000-STUDENT HEALTH CENTER (1 items) 1 530410-RESTRICTED ACCOUNTING (1 items) 1 530465-ACCOUNTING & FINANCIAL REPORTING (1 items) 1 920900-ALCC STUDENT SERVICES (1 items) 1 940675-DACC ARTS, HUMANITIES, SOC SCI DIV (1 items) 1 940690-DACC ENGLISH DEPT (1 items) 1 940695-DACC MATH AND STATISTICS DEPT (1 items) 1 940710-DACC EDUCATION PGM (1 items) 1 940725-DACC SOCIAL SCIENCES PGM (1 items) 1 940760-DACC LIBRARY (1 items) 1 940802-DACC HEATING AC AND REFRIG PGM (1 items) 1 940880-DACC SCIENCE, ENGINEERING, MATH DIV (1 items) 1 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS (1 items) 1 941230-DACC FACILITIES SUPP (1 items) 1 941600-DACC ADVISING SVCS (1 items) 1 950510-GRCC REG ACADEMIC INSTRUCTION (1 items) 1 950520-GRCC VOCATIONAL INSTRUCTION (1 items) 1 950850-GRCC STUDENT SERVICES CTR (1 items) 1 Employment Type Search employment types 8 filter options found Employment Type 12-Month Faculty Full-Time (3 items) 3 9-Month Faculty Full-Time (17 items) 17 Extension Agent/Specialist (5 items) 5 Post Doctoral (1 items) 1 Staff Full-time (54 items) 54 Staff Part-time (1 items) 1 Temporary Faculty (5 items) 5 Temporary Staff (3 items) 3 City Search cities 6 filter options found City Alamogordo Community College (1 items) 1 Doña Ana Community College (11 items) 11 Grants Community College (3 items) 3 Las Cruces (55 items) 55 NMSU satellite location (13 items) 13 Remote Locations (5 items) 5 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Las Cruces 331500-PHYSICS Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Physics at New Mexico State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics beginning in Fall 2027.\nWe seek outstanding candidates who will develop a vigorous externally funded research program and contribute to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education.\nNew Mexico State University is a Carnegie R1 research university located in Las Cruces, a vibrant city in southern New Mexico known for its outstanding climate, affordable cost of living, rich cultural diversity, outdoor recreation opportunities, and proximity to major national laboratories and research facilities. Read more Assistant Professor Las Cruces 331250-MATHEMATICAL SCIENCES Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Mathematical Sciences at New Mexico State University invites applicants for a tenure-track faculty appointment to be filled at the Assistant Professor level beginning Fall, 2027. The position will support research and teaching needs in the department, with research focus in Statistics. Individuals interested in contributing to a diverse academic community are particularly encouraged. Read more College Assistant Professor Las Cruces 331250-MATHEMATICAL SCIENCES Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time The Department of Mathematical Sciences at New Mexico State University invites applicants for a college-track faculty appointment to be filled at the Assistant Professor level beginning August 2027. The position will support the department's teaching needs; there is no research component. Individuals interested in contributing to a diverse academic community are particularly encouraged. Read more IPRA Records and Data Management Specialist Las Cruces 480200-UNIVERSITY GENERAL COUNSEL Staff Staff Full-time Join NMSU’s professional legal team and apply your analytical skills to respond to public records requests in a prompt, professional manner. In this job, you will work with legal assistants and attorneys to utilize specialized software and coordinate with stakeholders across campus to help ensure compliance with the Inspection of Public Records Act. You will additionally have the opportunity to use these skills to assist with litigation discovery and contribute to the legal team with other operational processes. Read more Administrative Assistant Associate NMSU satellite location 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Staff Staff Full-time Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Read more People Relations Consultant Las Cruces 510100-OFFICE OF PEOPLE RELATIONS Staff Staff Full-time This position will remain open until filled. Applications received within the first 14 days of the posting will receive first consideration.\n\nJoin a collaborative, innovative, and people-centered team at the Office of People Relations. Our work is driven by connection, purpose, and impact. As a member of the OPR team, you’ll play a vital role in building and strengthening relationships across the university, applying strong communication and problem-solving skills to support thoughtful, effective solutions.\n\nIn this role, you’ll draw on your interpersonal skills to navigate sensitive and complex situations, while using analytical skills to gather, assess, and interpret information that informs sound decision-making. If you’re passionate about people, value teamwork, and want to contribute to a workplace where your skills truly make a difference, we invite you to join us. Read more STEM Education Specialist Las Cruces 350410-INST FOR EXCEL IN MATH & SCIENCE ED Staff Staff Full-time The NMSU STEM Outreach Center is seeking STEM Education Specialists to advance STEM+ education across New Mexico by providing high-quality professional learning for PreK–12 educators, developing engaging inquiry-based curriculum, and supporting schools and communities in creating impactful STEM+ out-of-school time programs. Read more Research Integrity Coordinator Las Cruces 470300-RESEARCH ADMINISTRATION Staff Staff Full-time Join New Mexico State University's Research Administration team as a Research Integrity Coordinator.  Based in Las Cruces, the Research Integrity Coordinator implements and monitors components of oversight programs in the unit of Research Integrity and Compliance within the Research Administration Department.  Coordinates institutional-wide initiatives in one or more specialized areas, including the review boards for research with human participants, animals, bio-hazards, export controls, research security programs, and/or financial conflict of interest and commitment disclosures. Assists review committees by providing administrative management of electronic approval systems and record keeping.  Serves as a designated point of contact to respond to requests from faculty, staff, and students for guidance and training in compliance topics.  Provides timely and informed customer service.  Develops and implements training and written procedures for emerging regulatory issues. Read more Electromagnetic Engineer Las Cruces 470725-PSL TELEMETRY MISSILE SYSTEMS Staff Staff Full-time Join the PSL TMS team as an Electromagnetic Engineer! Read more Temporary Firefighter/EMT Las Cruces 500425-FIRE PROTECTION SERVICES Staff Temporary Staff Make a difference when it matters most! Join NMSU as a firefighter/EMS professional!\n\nThis is a temporary appointment with a predetermined end date not to exceed 1 year and is subject to an earlier termination if necessary. Temporary employees have no entitlement or expectation of continued employment during or beyond the appointment period. Read more NMDA Inspector Intermediate - Possible Career Development Opportunity Las Cruces 181150-NMDA PETROLEUM STANDARDS BUREAU Staff Staff Full-time The New Mexico Department of Agriculture (NMDA) works for the benefit of the state’s citizens and supports the viability of agriculture and affiliated industries. NMDA promotes food protection, a uniform, and fair marketplace, and global marketing and economic development; supports the beneficial use of natural resources; and works cooperatively with public and private sector entities. Opportunities for excellence abound, and NMDA staff dedicate themselves to proactive service in fulfilling the department’s mission. Each division plays an important role in carrying out the goals and objectives. Our rich agricultural history, culture, and traditions are addressed through new and innovative approaches using the latest in science, technology, and economic strategies. In New Mexico, we contribute to the safest and most affordable, and nutritious food supply on the globe.\n\nNMDA is a constitutional agency organized under the Board of Regents of New Mexico State University (NMSU). This unique relationship creates efficiencies and opportunities for New Mexico’s food and agriculture sector as well as service and outreach opportunities for NMSU, making NMDA an integral part of the university. NMDA/NMSU is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. Read more Associate Vice President for Research Las Cruces 470001-RESEARCH, CREATIVITY AND ED Staff Staff Full-time The Associate Vice President for Research (AVPR) is a senior leadership position within the\nOffice of the Vice President for Research (OVPR) at New Mexico State University (NMSU), an\nRl land-grant institution. Reporting to the Vice President for Research and serving as a key\nmember of the VPR leadership team, the AVPR provides strategic direction, operational\noversight, and institutional leadership to advance NMSU's research, innovation, and\neconomic development mission.\nThe AVPR plays a central role in strengthening research centers and institutes, expanding\nhigh-impact partnerships, enhancing research infrastructure, and fostering\ninterdisciplinary and convergent research. The position is critical to positioning NMSU for\nsuccess in large, complex, multi-institutional research initiatives and in strengthening\nengagement with national laboratories, academic institutions, and industry partners. Read more Research Assistant Senior Las Cruces 330350-BIOLOGY Post Doctoral Staff Full-time The Department of Biology is seeking applicants for a Research Assistant III. Read more Enterprise Instructional Technical Admin Inter Las Cruces 440410-DIGITAL LEARNING Staff Staff Full-time New Mexico State University’s Global Campus seeks an Enterpr Instr Tech Admin, Inter who will provide support, training, and professional development for faculty across the NMSU system, focusing on the Canvas Learning Management System. Responsibilities include staffing the online open lab, creating workshops and materials, and performing other related duties as assigned. This is a hybrid position based in Las Cruces, NM, and will require regular in-office presence. Read more Administrative Assistant Associate NMSU satellite location 317700-AG SCIENCE CTR AT FARMINGTON Staff Staff Full-time The New Mexico State University's Agricultural Experimental Station is seeking a dependable and organized Administrative Assistant II to provide administrative and operational support for the Agricultural Science Center in Farmington.  This position will assist with day-to-day office operations, purchasing, financial and personnel processes, recordkeeping, correspondence, scheduling, and customer service. Read more Fiscal Assistant Senior Las Cruces 300100-AG AND HOME ECON COL BUS RES PLNG Staff Staff Full-time The department of Agriculture and Home Economics College Business Resource Planning invites you to apply for the position of Fiscal Assistant III. Read more Research Scientist Senior NMSU satellite location 360200-CARLSBAD ENV MONITORING AND RES CTR Staff Staff Full-time Lead our vital radiochemistry program, ensuring the highest standards of analysis for environmental samples supporting the Department of Energy's Waste Isolation Pilot Plant (WIPP). You'll manage a dedicated team, provide expert technical guidance, and drive project success from development to reporting.\n\nWe're looking for a safety-conscious professional with extensive experience in radiochemical separation methods and a commitment to quality. If you're ready to contribute to groundbreaking research and thrive in a dynamic, hands-on environment, apply today! Read more Administrative Assistant Associate NMSU satellite location 312550-ADMIN AND PGM UNIT TAOS Staff Staff Full-time The New Mexico State University's Cooperative Extension Service is seeking a dependable and organized Administrative Assistant II to provide administrative and operational support for the Administrative and Program Unit in Taos. This position will assist with day-to-day office operations, purchasing, financial and personnel processes, recordkeeping, correspondence, scheduling, and customer service. Read more Administrative Assistant Associate NMSU satellite location 313350-ADMIN PRGM LINCOLN CTY Staff Staff Full-time The Cooperative Extension Service in Lincoln County is looking for a detailed-oriented administrative professional to handle a variety of essential tasks, including managing records, coordinating schedules, processing basic bookkeeping, arranging travel, and supporting office operations. Read more NMDA Agriculture Specialist Intermediate Las Cruces 180500-NMDA PESTICIDE MANAGEMENT BUREAU Staff Staff Full-time New Mexico Department of Agriculture (NMDA) works for the benefit of the state’s citizens and supports the viability of agriculture and affiliated industries. NMDA promotes food protection, a uniform and fair market place, and global marketing and economic development; supports beneficial use of natural resources; and works cooperatively with public and private sector entities. Opportunities for excellence abound, and NMDA staff dedicate themselves to proactive service in fulfilling the department’s mission. Each division plays an important role in carrying out the goals and objectives. Our rich agricultural history, culture, and traditions are addressed through new and innovative approaches using the latest in science, technology, and economic strategies. In New Mexico we contribute to the safest and most affordable and nutritious food supply on the globe.\n\nNMDA is a constitutional agency organized under the Board of regents of New Mexico State University (NMSU). This unique relationship creates efficiencies and opportunities for New Mexico’s food and agriculture sector as well as service and outreach opportunities for NMSU, making NMDA an integral part of the university. Read more NMDA Agriculture Specialist Intermediate Las Cruces 180100-NMDA ENTOMOL AND NURSERY IND BUREAU Staff Staff Full-time New Mexico Department of Agriculture (NMDA) works for the benefit of the state’s citizens and supports the viability of agriculture and affiliated industries. NMDA promotes food protection, a uniform and fair market place, and global marketing and economic development; supports beneficial use of natural resources; and works cooperatively with public and private sector entities. Opportunities for excellence abound, and NMDA staff dedicate themselves to proactive service in fulfilling the department’s mission. Each division plays an important role in carrying out the goals and objectives. Our rich agricultural history, culture, and traditions are addressed through new and innovative approaches using the latest in science, technology, and economic strategies. In New Mexico we contribute to the safest and most affordable and nutritious food supply on the globe.\n\nNMDA is a constitutional agency organized under the Board of regents of New Mexico State University (NMSU). This unique relationship creates efficiencies and opportunities for New Mexico’s food and agriculture sector as well as service and outreach opportunities for NMSU, making NMDA an integral part of the university. Read more Program Specialist Las Cruces 200113-ARROWHEAD CENTER Staff Staff Full-time At Arrowhead, we help innovators, entrepreneurs, and small businesses at any stage start and grow through our services, resources, expertise, and connections. \nAs the technology transfer and commercialization arm of NMSU, we partner with campus inventors and innovators to protect their intellectual property and bring their discoveries to the broadest possible markets.\nWhile we are proudly based at NMSU in Las Cruces, NM and are deeply engaged in our on-campus community, our reach extends across the state.  We providing guidance, mentorship, education, and hands-on experiences to support the development of new technologies, businesses, and partnerships. \nBe part of the team that drives innovation and creates opportunity, join us at Arrowhead! Read more Administrative Assistant Associate Las Cruces 500450-FS ACCOUNTING Staff Staff Full-time Join our team! Serve as the first point of contact for Facilities & Services, providing exceptional customer service, coordinating work orders, and processing access requests. Read more Technical Services Librarian Doña Ana Community College 940760-DACC LIBRARY Staff Staff Full-time DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Read more Nursing Laboratory Assistant Las Cruces 370200-NURSING Staff Staff Full-time The School of Nursing has a job opening for a Nursing Laboratory Assistant. Read more Enterprise Database Administrator Senior Las Cruces 450270-IT DATABASE ADMINISTRATION Staff Staff Full-time Join our team as a Senior Enterprise Database Administrator and play a critical role in powering the University's enterprise systems. Leverage your Oracle expertise to drive database performance, security, and reliability while supporting Banner ERP, cloud technologies, and data solutions that impact thousands of users across campus. Read more Police Department Support Services Coordinator Las Cruces 500300-POLICE DEPARTMENT NMSU Staff Staff Full-time Help keep the NMSU community safe while leading security operations for campus events, coordinating police and security personnel, and developing crime prevention initiatives. Come join our team and make a meaningful impact on campus safety! Read more Administrative Assistant Intermediate Las Cruces 522000-CORPORATE RELATIONS & CAREER EVENTS Staff Staff Full-time Join the Aggie Career Studio Team! \n\nAggie Career Studio at NMSU is looking for an organized, energetic, and service-minded Administrative Assistant who enjoys connecting with people and helping a team thrive.\n\nAs the welcoming face of the Career Studio, you’ll help create an engaging and supportive experience for students, employers, campus partners, and visitors. From coordinating day-to-day operations and supporting career events to assisting with communications, scheduling, and special projects, you’ll play an important role in keeping the Studio running smoothly and advancing our mission of preparing Aggies for career success.\n\nWe’re looking for someone who is proactive, dependable, detail-oriented, and comfortable juggling multiple priorities in a collaborative, student-centered environment. If you enjoy problem-solving, building relationships, staying organized, and being part of a team where every day brings something different, we’d love to hear from you!\n\nCome help us connect Aggies to opportunities and possibilities—one student, employer, and experience at a time. Read more Program Coordinator Las Cruces 317000-AGRICULTURAL EXPERIMENT STATION Staff Staff Part-time The Agricultural Experiment Station at New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator V to support the New Mexico Chile Association Center. This position is responsible for coordinating and managing program operations, fostering relationships with industry partners and stakeholders, overseeing administrative and fiscal activities, and supporting initiatives that advance and promote New Mexico’s chile industry. Read more Research Scientist Senior Remote Locations 317250-JORNADA EXPER RANGE HEADQUARTERS Staff Staff Full-time The Jornada Experimental Range is seeking applicants for a Senior Research Scientist with a focus on advancing next generation estimates of primary production in rangeland ecosystems. The successful candidate will lead efforts to critically evaluate and improve components of the Rangeland Analysis Platform (RAP) production model, including the MOD17 algorithm, field observations, and eddy flux data. There are also opportunities to explore applications of the RAP production data to grazing management. This position offers substantial intellectual freedom and the opportunity to innovate at the intersection of rangeland ecology and management, remote sensing, and earth systems modelling. Read more Displaying 31 - 60 of 88 in total ‹ 1 2 3 › Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status