s) 54 Staff Part-time (1 items) 1 Temporary Faculty (5 items) 5 Temporary Staff (3 items) 3 City Search cities 6 filter options found City Alamogordo Community College (1 items) 1 Doña Ana Community College (11 items) 11 Grants Community College (3 items) 3 Las Cruces (55 items) 55 NMSU satellite location (13 items) 13 Remote Locations (5 items) 5 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Academic Advisor Remote Locations 440100-NMSU GLOBAL Staff Staff Full-time Shifts: Sunday–Thursday, 8am-5pm MST\nLocation Preference: Preference given to candidates in Albuquerque, New Mexico, but available to any eligible states.\nWork Eligibility: Not eligible in CA, CO, IN, NJ, NY, OH, OR, PA, WA, or MN\nPlease Note: Travel and participation in in-person events are an integral part of supporting student and program success in this role.\nNew Mexico State University’s Global Campus seeks two Academic Advisors to guide and support adult learners, promoting retention, persistence, and overall student success. The position includes managing a caseload, collaborating across departments, and using technology to enhance the student experience. Preferred technical connectivity requirements are outlined in the Preferred Qualifications section. Read more Program Manager Senior Remote Locations 310021-EXTENSN HOME EC PGM UNIT Staff Staff Full-time The Center of Innovation (COI) is looking for a new High-Fidelity Wraparound Coach and Trainer to serve New Mexico Providers. The COI provides training and program implementation support throughout New Mexico to strengthen and expand the behavioral health and other child and family-serving systems in New Mexico. Read more Plumber Las Cruces 500770-FS MECHANICAL Staff Staff Full-time Join our team! We're hiring a Plumber to install, maintain, and repair water, gas, drainage, and steam systems. Requires NM Journeyman Plumbing or Gas Fitter License, or ability to obtain within one year from date of hire. Read more Plumber Lead Las Cruces 500770-FS MECHANICAL Staff Staff Full-time Join our team! Lead and support plumbers and trade workers in the repair, maintenance, and installation of campus plumbing systems. Plan schedules, inspect work, estimate materials and labor, and ensure timely project completion. Read more Business Manager Doña Ana Community College 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS Staff Staff Full-time DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Read more Program Manager Senior Remote Locations 310021-EXTENSN HOME EC PGM UNIT Staff Staff Full-time The Center of Innovation (COI) is looking for a trainer and program support professional for Family Peer, Youth Peer, Foster Care Connect and related programs. The COI provides training and program implementation support throughout New Mexico to strengthen and expand the behavioral health and other child and family-serving systems in New Mexico. Read more Agricultural Science Center Laborer NMSU satellite location 317700-AG SCIENCE CTR AT FARMINGTON Staff Staff Full-time The New Mexico State University Agricultural Science Center at Farmington is seeking an Agricultural Science Center Laborer to assist with the daily operations and maintenance of agricultural research and demonstration activities. Read more Steamfitter Las Cruces 500770-FS MECHANICAL Staff Staff Full-time Join our team! Maintain and repair campus steam distribution systems and operate high/low pressure boilers. Perform troubleshooting and preventative maintenance. Requires NM Journeyman Pipe Fitter (JFP) License or ability to obtain License within year from date of hire. Read more Ext Ag/4-H Agent NMSU satellite location 310500-ADMIN PRGM DE BACA CTY Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Ag/4-H Agent to serve De Baca County. This position provides an exciting opportunity to work directly with youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members through educational programming and outreach. Read more Facilities Technician Senior Doña Ana Community College 941230-DACC FACILITIES SUPP Staff Staff Full-time DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following four (4) available Facilities Technician Sr positions Read more Admissions Advisor Associate Alamogordo Community College 920900-ALCC STUDENT SERVICES Staff Staff Full-time Are you passionate about education, community engagement, and helping students achieve their goals?New Mexico State University–Alamogordo (NMSU-A) is seeking a dynamic, motivated Admissions Advisor to join our team! Read more Ext 4H Agent NMSU satellite location 312200-ADMIN PRGM RIO ARRIBA CTY Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist The Cooperative Extension Service at NMSU is excited to announce an opening for a 4H Agent for Rio Arriba County, NM. If you have a passion for 4-H Youth Development Programming in the areas of Ag and Natural Resources, please apply today. Read more Academic Department Head/Agricultural & Extension Education Las Cruces 300400-AGRICULTURAL AND EXTENSION EDUC Faculty 12-Month Faculty Full-Time We are seeking candidates with an understanding of and appreciation for undergraduate/graduate education, research, and outreach, with a strong commitment to the Land Grant mission. Read more Financial Aid Advisor Las Cruces 521040-UNIV FIN AID & SCHOLARSHIP SVCS Staff Staff Full-time The University Financial Aid and Scholarship Services department is seeking a highly motivated student centered individual with excellent customer service skills to join the Financial Aid Team. Read more Academic Advisor Education Doña Ana Community College 941600-DACC ADVISING SVCS Staff Staff Full-time DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Read more Health Education Specialist Las Cruces 523000-STUDENT HEALTH CENTER Staff Staff Full-time Help shape the future of student well-being at New Mexico State University. As a member of the newly established Aggie Prevention & Well-Being Programs team, you'll develop innovative health education programs, inspire healthy choices, and make a meaningful difference in the lives of Aggies every day. Read more Administrative Assistant Intermediate Las Cruces 521010-UNDERGRAD ADMISSIONS & ORIENTATION Staff Staff Full-time Aggie Welcome & Orientation (AWO) is a unit within the Department of Student Life that is seeking a positive and motivated individual to work as our inaugural Administrative Assistant. The unit is responsible for new student orientation, family engagement events throughout the year, and supporting both students and families in their transition to college/NMSU. AWO serves all students and families at the university and collaborates with other offices and programs to create a welcoming environment, and increase student success and retention. Read more Police Officer Las Cruces 500300-POLICE DEPARTMENT NMSU Staff Staff Full-time Join our campus police team and make a difference by protecting our community through proactive patrol, law enforcement, crime prevention, and community engagement in a dynamic and rewarding public safety role. Read more Ext Family Consumer Sci Agent NMSU satellite location 311800-ADMIN PRGM BERNIL CTY Faculty Extension Agent/Specialist The Cooperative Extension Service at New Mexico State University (NMSU) invites applications for a Family and Consumer Sciences Cooperative Extension Agent – Community and Food Entrepreneurship serving Bernalillo County, New Mexico. As the state's largest and most diverse urban county, Bernalillo County offers a unique opportunity to develop innovative, research-based educational programs that strengthen local communities and support economic opportunity.\n \nThis position will play a key role in helping entrepreneurs and small food businesses navigate and capitalize on New Mexico's recently expanded Cottage Food laws, which now allow the sale of a wider variety of shelf-stable food products. The successful candidate will provide education, technical assistance, and community outreach to aspiring and existing food entrepreneurs, helping them understand food safety, regulatory requirements, business development, and marketing strategies that contribute to sustainable economic growth.\n \nIn addition to supporting local food enterprises, the Family and Consumer Sciences Agent will deliver practical, research-based programming that empowers individuals, families, and communities to improve their quality of life through education, partnerships, and engagement. This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful impact by fostering entrepreneurship, enhancing food system resilience, and advancing community and economic development throughout Bernalillo County. Read more Academic Department Head Las Cruces 350500-DEPARTMENT OF KINESIOLOGY Faculty 12-Month Faculty Full-Time The College of Health, Education, and Social Transformation (HEST) at New Mexico State University invites nominations and applications for the position of Department Head of Kinesiology. This is an opportunity to lead a thriving academic department that combines outstanding faculty, exceptional students, nationally recognized academic programs, expanding research infrastructure, and a mission that directly improves the health and well-being of communities throughout the U.S.-Mexico Borderland.\n\nThe successful candidate will join New Mexico State University at an exciting moment in its history. As New Mexico's land-grant university and a Carnegie-designated Research 1 institution, NMSU is committed to research excellence, student success, innovation, and public engagement. The Department of Kinesiology has experienced sustained growth in enrollment, academic programming, and research capacity, and is well positioned for continued national prominence.\n\nThe Department of Kinesiology combines many of the characteristics that outstanding academic leaders seek:\n•\ta supportive college and university administration;\n•\texceptional faculty committed to teaching, scholarship, and service;\n•\tapproximately 600 undergraduate and graduate students;\n•\t17 full-time faculty members representing diverse areas of expertise;\n•\tstrong undergraduate, professional master's, and doctoral programs;\n•\tsignificant recent investments in research and instructional facilities.\n\nThe next Department Head will inherit a department with tremendous momentum. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to recruit outstanding faculty, strengthen nationally recognized research programs, expand interdisciplinary collaborations, enhance graduate education, and position the department among the leading kinesiology programs in the western United States. Read more Post Doctoral Las Cruces 331250-MATHEMATICAL SCIENCES Post Doctoral Staff Post Doctoral Staff Full-time The Department of Mathematical Sciences at New Mexico State University invites applicants for a two-year postdoctoral appointment beginning August, 2027. The position will support the research and teaching needs of the department. Individuals interested in contributing to a diverse academic community are particularly encouraged. Read more Temporary Security Officer Las Cruces 500300-POLICE DEPARTMENT NMSU Temporary Staff Temporary Staff This is a temporary appointment with a predetermined end date not to exceed 1 year and is subject to an earlier termination if necessary. Temporary employees have no entitlement or expectation of continued employment during or beyond the appointment period. Read more Temporary Public Safety Aide Parking Enforcement Officer Las Cruces 500300-POLICE DEPARTMENT NMSU Temporary Staff Temporary Staff This is a temporary appointment with a predetermined end date not to exceed 1 year and is subject to an earlier termination if necessary. Temporary employees have no entitlement or expectation of continued employment during or beyond the appointment period. Read more DACC Part-Time Faculty Early Childhood and Education Doña Ana Community College 940710-DACC EDUCATION PGM Temporary Faculty Temporary Faculty Join our team! Read more DACC Part-Time Faculty Humanities Department Doña Ana Community College 940675-DACC ARTS, HUMANITIES, SOC SCI DIV Temporary Faculty Temporary Faculty Join our team! Read more DACC Part-Time Faculty English Department Doña Ana Community College 940690-DACC ENGLISH DEPT Temporary Faculty Temporary Faculty Join our team! Read more DACC Part-Time Faculty Social Sciences Department Doña Ana Community College 940725-DACC SOCIAL SCIENCES PGM Temporary Faculty Temporary Faculty Join our team! Read more DACC Part Time Faculty Mathematics Doña Ana Community College 940695-DACC MATH AND STATISTICS DEPT Temporary Faculty Temporary Faculty Join our team! Read more Displaying 61 - 88 of 88 in total ‹ 1 2 3 › Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience